.TH SAVETOA 1 "September 2026" "savetoa 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
savetoa \- job-driven backup orchestrator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B savetoa
.RI [ \-\-config " path" ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.PP
.B savetoa
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
SaveToA coordinates named backup targets. A target selects a capture driver,
source settings and credentials, transformations, destinations, and retention
policy.
.PP
This release implements physical MariaDB, full+oplog MongoDB, and fresh-RDB Redis capture, verified local storage,
idempotent S3 delivery and recovery, target-scoped retention, and
safe materialization of completed local backup sets. Standalone listing and
verification commands fail explicitly until implemented.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Read configuration from
.I path
instead of
.IR /etc/savetoa/config.yml .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI run " target"
Capture and deliver one configured MariaDB, MongoDB, or Redis target to its local and S3 destinations.
The command performs driver-specific replica health checks and capture,
optional zstd and age transforms, durable staging, and destination verification.
.TP
.BI deliver " target destination backup-id"
Retry an S3 destination from a completed set in the durable spool. Existing
objects are accepted only when their bytes match, and the completion marker is
published last. No new capture or encryption is performed.
.TP
.B fetch
.RI [ --spool-root " root" ]
.I "target s3-source backup-id"
.br
Verify a completed S3 set and atomically import it into the durable spool. The
completion marker and canonical manifest are validated before the payload is
requested; payload size and checksum are verified before local publication.
An identical completed local set is reused and a conflict is never replaced.
The spool root defaults to
.IR /var/lib/savetoa/spool .
.TP
.BI run-group " group"
Run a configured group of targets.
.TP
.B list
List completed backup sets.
.TP
.BI verify " backup-id"
Verify a completed backup set.
.TP
.B restore
.BI \-\-source-root " root"
.BI \-\-target-dir " directory"
.RI [ \-\-identity-file " file" ]
.I backup-id
.br
Verify and materialize a completed local backup set into a new explicit
directory. Encrypted sets require a regular, non-symlink identity file with
mode 0600. This command does not activate or replace a database service.
.TP
.B restore-mongodb
.BI \-\-source-root " root"
.BI \-\-target-dir " directory"
.RI [ \-\-identity-file " file" ]
.I backup-id
.br
Verify a MongoDB backup and replay its archive and oplog into a temporary
loopback-only mongod using a new dbpath inside the explicit target directory.
The command does not accept a database endpoint and stops the disposable
server before reporting success.
.TP
.B restore-redis
.BI \-\-source-root " root"
.BI \-\-target-dir " directory"
.RI [ \-\-identity-file " file" ]
.I backup-id
.br
Verify a Redis backup and load its RDB into a temporary loopback-only
redis-server inside the explicit target directory. AOF and automatic saves are
disabled, no database endpoint is accepted, and the process is stopped before
success is reported.
.TP
.B prune
.RI [ --spool-root " root" ]
.I target
.br
Apply the configured UTC daily, ISO-weekly, and monthly retention policy to
the durable spool and every target destination. Every repository is validated
and planned before deletion begins. Incomplete sets are ignored; an invalid
completed set aborts planning. Deletion removes the completion marker first.
.TP
.BI doctor " target"
Validate a target and its dependencies without capturing data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/savetoa/config.yml
System-wide target configuration.
.TP
.I /etc/savetoa/credentials.d/
Protected source and destination credential files.
.TP
.I /etc/savetoa/recipients.d/
Client-side encryption recipients.
.TP
.I /etc/savetoa/maintenance-credentials.d/
Protected S3 list/delete credentials, inaccessible to backup units.
.TP
.I /var/lib/savetoa/
Persistent state, work directories, and delivery spool.
.TP
.I /var/backups/savetoa/
Default local backup destination.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/bionicman/savetoa/issues.
